  "heading": "Lesson Eleven: Invalidators of prayer",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "They are eight:"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "1. Intentional talking while remembering and being aware (of its prohibition). However, the prayer of the one who forgot or was unaware (of its prohibition) is not invalidated by that."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "2. Laughing."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "3. Eating."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "4. Drinking."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "5. Exposure of ‘Awrah (must-cover body parts)."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "6. Excessive diversion from the Qiblah direction."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "7. Excessive and continuous fiddling during the prayer."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "pages": [
        17
      ],
      "text": "8. Nullification of Tahārah (ritual purity)."
    }
  ],
